00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.790
"Pokee," you say?

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.620
They're the standard when it comes to snacks.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.620
They're just so crunchy and delicious!

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:10.790
I know of them! I've heard that in Japan,

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:10.790
friends will engage in a Pokee game!

00:04:10.950 --> 00:04:13.500
Huh? A Pokee game...?

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.500
Do you know what sort of game it is, UMR?

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.500
Huh?! Uh, I think so...

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:23.250
Impressive, indeed!

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:27.450
In that case, I would like to do it with you,

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:27.450
this so-called Pokee game!

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:28.160
What?!

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:36.750
Japan's

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:33.040
U-uh, no, no way! That's not a game that we would play.

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:36.620
Why not?! I wish to do it with you, indeed!

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.160
The thing about the Pokee game, is, um...

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:44.330
Ah! You have to do it with someone

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:44.330
who's really SPECIAL to you.

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:49.660
But I think of you as a MOST special friend, UMR!

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:56.080
I-I think the same of you, but there's NO WAY

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:56.080
we're playing the Pokee game!

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:01.540
Oh. Sorry for raising my voice like that...

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:05.370
it's just, I don't think that's the kind of game

00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:05.370
that friends play with each other.

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:13.580
No, it's all right. It's my fault for getting carried away

00:05:05.790 --> 00:05:13.580
at having a friend over.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.750
Oh. I see...

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:20.950
it's nice having this big room and all,

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:20.950
but I bet it's lonely having her snack feasts all by herself.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:28.250
Japan's

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:28.250
Best

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:24.700
Really, I'm the one who's sorry.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:28.120
Um... you're a great friend, TSF!

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.500
Yes!

00:05:31.000 --> 00:05:33.580
For some reason, I'm SUPER embarrassed!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.250
Oh, yeah. Let's watch some anime.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:43.870
Hey! Let's play the Pokee game!

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:50.410
Ah! They play the Pokee game even in anime.

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:50.410
I wonder what sort of game it is, indeed!

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:55.370
Well, here goes. We each take one end, and then...

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:00.290
But, we're getting closer and closer!

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:15.790
U-um, so, that's why... we can't do it, right?

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:15.790
The Pokee game.

00:06:16.160 --> 00:06:19.000
A-agreed! My apologies!

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.700
Oh, hi there, Hikari.

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:31.370
S-sorry to put you out, Big Brother.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.200
She really did come for bread day, Big Brother.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:37.830
I'm glad I made enough for the three of us.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.120
Today, I've made curry and naan.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:42.000
The deuce, you say!

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.410
It's nice and chewy!

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:48.540
It is!

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:49.410
Glad to hear it...

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:54.540
So, Hikari, Kanau knows you've been coming here, right?

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:56.830
Yes!

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.000
Like I thought, she doesn't know...

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:00.750
Kanau!

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.660
Taihei?! C-can I help you?

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:07.330
Sorry about before. It took longer

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:07.330
than expected to wrap things up.

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:09.750
Huh? Wrap up...?

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:12.580
Note: Kanau mistakenly confuses the meaning of "to get someone home,"

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:12.580
for the homophone "to return something."

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:12.580
RETURN

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:15.870
Note: Kanau mistakenly confuses the meaning of "to get someone home,"

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:15.870
for the homophone "to return something."

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:15.870
Did I lend you something?

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:16.750
Huh?

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:17.620
Hmm?

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:25.160
Umaruuun!

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.080
Umaruu                                                        uuuuuun

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:31.450
Hikari, is it possible you've been coming here without

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:31.450
saying anything? That would make your sister worry...

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.870
Say, Big Brother, why don't you call her?

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:38.870
Gah! Th-there's no need!

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:45.080
Well, it IS more dangerous at night,

00:07:40.160 --> 00:07:45.080
and she's probably made dinner already...

00:07:54.290 --> 00:08:00.620
My sister works overtime on Tuesdays.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:08:00.620
I've just been eating on my own.

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.750
Oh, really? Well, we don't mind at all!

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:09.910
I'll be working late tonight,

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:09.910
but I've made dinner and put it in the fridge.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:13.580
Huh? I've gotta eat alone?

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:15.580
Well, fine, if there's no other option...

00:08:15.580 --> 00:08:16.540
Huh?

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:18.830
Hurry up or it'll get cold.

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:19.790
Okay.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:24.910
You sure you don't need me to walk you home?

00:08:24.910 --> 00:08:27.910
No, I'm meeting someone, so I'll be fine.

00:08:29.000 --> 00:08:34.000
U-um, Big Brother? Is it all right if I come again?

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:37.250
Well, yeah, I guess.

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:39.580
Come whenever you like, Hikari.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.660
Okay!

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.870
Just don't make a habit of coming every week, yeah?

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:47.160
RRRRRRUMBLE

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:46.830
I shall.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:27.000
Hey! What are you doing, Hikari?!

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:33.540
I'm home, Hikari.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:35.120
Welcome back, Big Sis.

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:38.750
Hikari! You went out tonight, didn't you?!

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.540
Liar! I know you've been going out

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.540
on Tuesdays when I work overtime!

00:09:44.540 --> 00:09:47.540
I-I only went to get something to eat.

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:50.620
It's dangerous to be out this late, okay?!

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:55.160
I thought for sure you'd object when Hikari said

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:55.160
she wanted to come over again.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:57.080
N-nah, I don't really mind...

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:05.410
Oh, my!

00:10:05.410 --> 00:10:08.120
Hm? What is it, TSF?

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:12.500
UMR, didn't this used to be a beauty shop?

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:16.790
Hey, you're right! TSF, had you been here before?

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:20.750
No. But it had an old-timey feel, and I liked it, indeed!

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:26.120
It's indeed a shame when a shop you like goes away...

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:31.290
You do like retro-style buildings,

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:31.290
don't you? I do too, I guess.

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:34.870
Still, you sure know a lot about old-school

00:10:31.700 --> 00:10:34.870
department stores and candy shops,

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:37.580
even though you lived in Germany.

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:39.950
I do! Such things are nostalgic, indeed!

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:43.040
"Nostalgic"? You've got

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:43.040
the same kind of stuff in Germany?

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:48.120
Well, no. But I'd been to Japan once before.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.250
When I was six, I made quite the fuss

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:52.250
until I was brought here for some sightseeing!

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:55.870
Making such a fuss that they brought her

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:55.870
from Germany here to Japan is pretty impressive...

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:02.080
And when I came, I saw an old arcade

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:02.080
with a beautiful lake and a giant swan.

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:05.700
It's a wonderful memory, one that I've kept to this day.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:11.580
Well, do you want to head out there today?

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:16.910
That's all right. I don't remember where it is,

00:11:11.580 --> 00:11:16.910
and I doubt it exists anymore.

00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:18.660
No, it's still there.

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:19.450
Hm?

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:22.870
I think it's probably that mecca for retro gamers.

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:30.080
I'm somewhat afraid, UMR.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:30.950
Hm?

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:37.410
If the scenery has changed from how I remember it...

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:37.410
I think it would be a bit of a shock.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:39.750
Don't you worry, TSF.

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:43.830
SAGAMIKO

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:43.410
Staying the same is what makes the mecca a mecca.

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:45.700
Whaaat?!

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:46.950
BOAT

00:11:45.700 --> 00:11:46.950
GUIDE

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:48.290
I-it can't be...

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:50.950
It's completely unchanged!

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:51.870
Exactly.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:54.950
Sagamiko Park hasn't changed a bit.

00:11:55.370 --> 00:11:56.750
The buildings are the same...

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.540
Even the signs are the same!

00:11:57.410 --> 00:11:58.830
RBI CHAMP

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:01.500
Welcome.

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.120
Ten

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.120
Years

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.120
Ago

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:08.370
It's the same store employee!

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.450
Look! It's the all-important pinball!

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:16.200
Indeed, even that is the same as back then!

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:22.370
Ah, there you are!

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:24.660
Big Brother!

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.000
Hurry up. The Swan Boat is gonna leave!

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:28.200
Okay!

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:36.540
TSF, there's a rare game over here

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:36.540
that I've never seen before!

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.410
Okay!

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:47.750
It looks like most of the people

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:47.750
on those boats are couples.

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:49.370
Yes, indeed!

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.080
Sylph, why don't you want to leave?

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:59.660
Because after today, we'll go back to Germany!

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:04.250
And I... I won't be able to see Big Brother anymore!

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:05.200
Sylphin.

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:08.910
Brother?

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.200
She hasn't said a word since I mentioned couples...

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:17.040
TSF? What's the matter?

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:20.370
UMR, let's ride one of those boats!

00:13:20.370 --> 00:13:21.080
Huh?!

00:13:21.290 --> 00:13:23.250
THAT'S where this conversation led to?

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:28.830
Hup! Whoa! This thing is shaky!

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:32.250
This is the first time I've been on a boat.

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:36.620
You're my all-knowing hero, UMR. You'll be fine indeed!

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:41.370
I'm hardly all-knowing. I only knew about

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:41.370
the Sagamiko arcade because it's famous.

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:42.620
UMR!

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:43.330
Hm?

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:47.540
Thank you so much for coming for me!

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:52.750
Don't you mean, "Thank you for BRINGING me?"

00:13:53.120 --> 00:13:55.370
I think it's perfectly fitting, indeed!

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:59.290
Let's do this again. I'll come for you.

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:00.290
Okay!

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:06.950
MIDTERMS (DAY 1)

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:06.950
ENGLISH

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.950
MATH

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.950
LANGUAGE ARTS

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.910
Tests start tomorrow, huh?

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:06.830
It's been a while, indeed!

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:09.620
Are you feeling confident, Umaru?

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:11.830
There sure is a lot we have to know this time...

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.830
Hm? What is it, Ebina?

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:23.250
I think I'm going to fail tomorrow's tests...

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:23.250
I might not even make it to the next grade!

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:24.370
Huh?

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:27.500
What did you mean, you won't make it to the next grade?

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:31.580
B-but this is the day before exams!

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:31.580
Why are you only now...?!

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:37.910
The timing just didn't feel right.

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:37.910
I hope I pass along with the rest of you, but maybe I...

00:14:38.200 --> 00:14:39.330
Ebina...

00:14:42.160 --> 00:14:45.250
If that's what is at stake here, then this where I come in!

00:14:45.250 --> 00:14:46.370
SHBAFUUUN

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:49.290
We shall hold a study group, indeed!

00:14:49.410 --> 00:14:51.410
Th-this is one amazing library...

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:56.910
There is a wealth of books here,

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:56.910
and the silence most certainly lends itself to study!

00:14:57.290 --> 00:14:58.910
What do you think, Umaru?

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.330
I-it's great!

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:03.870
I've never even been in here...

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:08.330
I'm thrilled at the idea of having

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:08.330
a study session with you all!

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:11.080
Um, I don't think this is the right time to feel "thrilled."

00:15:11.540 --> 00:15:14.700
Ebina, what would you say are your weakest subjects?

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.620
A-all of them.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:17.620
All of them?!

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:20.830
Well, let's just see how things go.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:24.330
Ebina...

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.660
You have a pretty decent grasp of this.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:28.500
U-um...

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:32.870
This will be enough to get you

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:32.870
about an 80. Thank goodness.

00:15:33.120 --> 00:15:36.330
Ebina, I think you have performance anxiety.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:43.790
That time before when we studied together,

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:43.790
you did just fine...

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:47.580
But later, when we took the test,

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:47.580
it looked like you didn't do so well.

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:53.040
Everyone gets so serious when we're taking tests...

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:53.040
it's like a totally different classroom!

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:57.660
It's as if I'm the only one

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:57.660
who gets left behind by the flow of time...

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:02.500
Reckon things could go wrong at the drop of a hat,

00:15:58.290 --> 00:16:02.500
and I'd just wanna up and go back to Akita!

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:04.200
I know, right?

00:16:04.370 --> 00:16:06.790
Th-that must mean some seriously bad grades!

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:11.660
S-so then, so long as you're not nervous,

00:16:07.250 --> 00:16:11.660
you should be able to get a passing grade, right?

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:14.790
Yeah, but... what should we do?

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:19.750
I personally think of people as vegetables

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:19.750
or something and purge them from my mind.

00:16:19.750 --> 00:16:21.410
She always does that?!

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:26.250
You know, you may be able to relax

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:26.250
if you think about something you like.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:27.700
Something I like...

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:34.540
Th-th-that might make me worry even MORE!

00:16:34.540 --> 00:16:36.250
Did she imagine something?

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:42.330
Still, this is sort of vexing. The test is tomorrow,

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:42.330
but we haven't found a way to solve things.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:47.200
You all have your own studying to do,

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:47.200
but you're taking the time to help ME...

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:50.290
I'm sorry! I'm just dragging you all down.

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:54.370
I-in any case, right now

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:54.370
we need less tears and more ideas!

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:58.950
Indeed, that's right! We're sure to find

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:58.950
a sound solution if we put our heads together.

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:01.700
Come on, Ebina. Wipe those tears.

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:09.620
E-everyone, why are you...?

00:17:09.950 --> 00:17:11.450
Because we're friends!

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:12.750
Y'know?

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:14.040
Indeed!

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:16.040
It's only natural, wouldn't you say?

00:17:18.250 --> 00:17:20.870
Okay, let's start memorizing, Ebina!

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:24.080
Sylphin, that's not the subject for tomorrow's test.

00:17:25.370 --> 00:17:27.200
In that case, learn THIS!

00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:28.330
That's not right, either.

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:30.620
Jeez... Sylphin, you're hopeless.

00:17:33.410 --> 00:17:35.700
My first day at a new school...

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:38.660
I-I'm kinda nervous!

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:41.500
So, you're from the Midwest?

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:44.500
That's right. It's nice to meet you!

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:45.660
I'm from the Northwest!

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:49.250
Those girls over there've already made friends!

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:54.500
I-I want some friends too.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:54.500
Reckon I gotta talk to someone!

00:17:56.540 --> 00:17:58.950
Maybe I'll try talking to her.

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:04.120
That Motoba girl kinda lost it

00:17:59.580 --> 00:18:04.120
at the entrance ceremony, huh?

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:07.160
Got that right. They say

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:07.160
she kicked some guy, a grownup!

00:18:17.120 --> 00:18:19.250
Oh. She left...

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:23.080
Maybe I'll try inviting her out for lunch sometime.

00:18:25.540 --> 00:18:26.120
Hm?

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:29.000
It is a pleasure to meet you all!

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:35.120
My name is Sylphinford Tachibana, and I shall become

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:35.120
the greatest "player" in this classroom, indeed!

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:36.370
Shbafeeeen!

00:18:35.200 --> 00:18:36.370
SHBAFEEE                             EEEEEEEN

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:40.620
Sh-she's... like... outta some magazine!

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:43.620
I think I'll be able to talk to her, though.

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:48.910
U-um, it's nice to meet you. Ebina is my name.

00:18:48.910 --> 00:18:52.620
"Ebina S. Maineim"? That's a rather unusual name.

00:18:52.830 --> 00:18:55.410
Um, no, I...

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:56.580
It's "Ebina."

00:18:56.790 --> 00:19:02.790
And yet! You're quite courageous to be the first one

00:18:56.790 --> 00:19:02.790
to come talk to me. That is the spirit, indeed!

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:05.580
I challenge you, Ebimori!

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:06.870
It's "Ebina"...

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:09.750
U-um, a challenge?

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:13.700
Yes, at whatever you would say you are best at.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:13.700
Come at me with anything!

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:16.910
Maybe challenges like this are normal in Tokyo.

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:24.870
As for what I'm "best at"... I'm no good at studying,

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:24.870
though I'm not bad at cooking and household chores...

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:28.120
Still, I can't do those now.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.500
I can eat a lot of akitakomachi rice!

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:37.540
But we don't have any akitakomoachi...

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.120
Have you decided?

00:19:39.120 --> 00:19:41.000
Um...!

00:19:41.000 --> 00:19:41.830
'Morning.

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.080
Umaruuuun!

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.160
Umaruuu                                                     uuuuun

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:50.200
She...

00:19:50.200 --> 00:19:52.200
Reckon she's like a princess and all!

00:19:56.040 --> 00:20:01.080
You are Umaru Doma, yes? I heard you took

00:19:56.040 --> 00:20:01.080
the top spot in the entrance exams.

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:05.040
Um, I don't know if I was at the top or not...

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:07.500
You will now challenge me, please!

00:20:07.500 --> 00:20:08.160
Huh?

00:20:08.330 --> 00:20:10.750
So her name's "Umaru Doma."

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:14.830
Come now, be quick! It's a challenge!

00:20:10.950 --> 00:20:14.830
A challenge, indeed!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:19.040
Wonder if maybe one day me

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:19.040
and these girls can be friends...

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:23.950
Ebina?

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:26.370
Huh? Um, what?

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:29.540
You okay? It looked like you were spacing out.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:33.750
Ah! I'm so sorry!

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:41.370
Hm? What is it? What's the matter?

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:44.410
It's because Sylphin keeps acting all weird.

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:46.370
So now I am the cause?

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:52.000
It's nothing. Really, it's nothing.

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:53.660
Umaru...

00:20:53.910 --> 00:20:54.660
Hm?

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:56.290
Kirie...

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:57.370
Huh?

00:20:57.620 --> 00:20:58.700
Sylphin...

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:00.000
Yes?

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:02.200
Let's all study together!

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:08.500
Okay!

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.910
MIDTERMS (DAY 1)

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.910
ENGLISH

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.910
MATH

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.910
LANGUAGE ARTS

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:12.660
All right, start your tests.

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:24.370
Even more...

00:21:24.750 --> 00:21:27.500
Now and forever...

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.540
I want to be with my friends!

00:21:36.290 --> 00:21:38.200
Ebina, let's go home together.

00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:39.120
Sure!

00:21:39.830 --> 00:21:43.500
Kirie, I'll race you to that utility pole over there!

00:21:43.500 --> 00:21:46.870
Wh-why would I want to do something like that?

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:49.580
Because seeing who comes first

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:49.580
would be a challenge indeed!

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:53.580
H-how about we all go eat some crêpes or something?

00:21:56.290 --> 00:21:58.040
Okay, let’s start with warmups!

00:21:58.410 --> 00:22:00.870
Stretch your hands out straight and shake them around

00:22:00.870 --> 00:22:02.700
Here we go! Starting from the right

00:22:02.910 --> 00:22:03.700
One, two!

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:06.000
Puura puraa, puura puraa, puura puraa puuraa

00:22:03.700 --> 00:22:06.000
Shake, shake, shake-shake-shake, shake

00:22:06.000 --> 00:22:06.540
Left!

